ms_invoice_flow__1.content:
Found it in `services/billing/src/subscribers/orderDelivered.ts`. The subscriber is registered from `services/billing/src/index.ts` via `registerOrderDeliveredSubscriber(eventBus, billingApp)`. It subscribes to `order.delivered` and calls `CreateInvoice`:

```ts
// services/billing/src/subscribers/orderDelivered.ts
export function registerOrderDeliveredSubscriber(bus: EventBus, app: BillingApp) {
  bus.subscribe('order.delivered', async (evt: OrderDeliveredEvent) => {
    await app.commands.CreateInvoice.execute({
      orderId: evt.orderId,
      customerId: evt.customerId,
      deliveredAt: evt.deliveredAt,
      idempotencyKey: `order:${evt.orderId}:invoice`
    })
  })
}
```

So the billing-service subscribes to `order.delivered` and generates the invoice via `CreateInvoice` with an idempotency key derived from the order ID.

Added `services/billing/test/subscribers/orderDelivered.test.ts` covering duplicate delivery events:

```ts
it('uses an order-derived idempotency key when creating invoices', async () => {
